<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIA'S AWB SELLS 9,000/T WHEAT IN TENDER 32.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIA'S AWB SELLS 9,000/T WHEAT IN TENDER 32.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said on Thursday it had sold 9,000 tonnes of wheat in its latest tender for domestic sales from the national pool.</p>
<p>Total bids were received for 149,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>In this, bids were for 13,000 tonnes of current season wheat and 136,000 tonnes of new crop wheat. Lowest successful bids were priced at A$210.00 a tonne for Australian Standard White (ASW) current crop delivered Geelong and Port Adelaide.  </p>
